One meal. That's all I'm asking for. Please?

249
00:15:36,970 --> 00:15:38,470
We go out, we eat.

250
00:15:38,640 --> 00:15:42,270
If you don't have a good time, I'll give you 10 grand, we're even.

251
00:15:52,860 --> 00:15:55,070
- Hi.     - Aah! No!

252
00:15:55,240 --> 00:15:58,240
Wait, no. Just put the mail down. It's me.

253
00:15:59,620 --> 00:16:02,830
Sorry. Why were you just all in the dark?

254
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:08,170
Well, um, your laundry smelled so good that I thought I'd curl up in it.

255
00:16:08,340 --> 00:16:10,380
- Is that all right?     - Yeah, sure.

256
00:16:10,550 --> 00:16:12,170
So how was your day?

257
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:16,140
It's just probably the worst one since I've been alive.

258
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:20,390
What, um...? What happened?

259
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:22,770
Um, Alice, uh...

260
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:25,190
She, uh, called it off.

261
00:16:25,350 --> 00:16:26,900
Oh, no.

262
00:16:29,270 --> 00:16:31,570
Did, um... Did she say why?

263
00:16:31,740 --> 00:16:34,570
Uh, no, not really. Just that I was too young.

264
00:16:34,740 --> 00:16:37,570
I don't see how I could suddenly be too young...

265
00:16:37,740 --> 00:16:41,200
...because I'm older than I was when we first got together.

266
00:16:42,830 --> 00:16:45,210
Yeah, yeah, no, I don't...

267
00:16:45,370 --> 00:16:50,210
I don't know. But you know what? Maybe it's just all for the best.

268
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:53,970
Well, yeah, if the best is like unbelievable pain.

269
00:16:54,130 --> 00:16:56,260
Oh, sweetie.

270
00:16:56,890 --> 00:16:59,720
You know, I was just finally happy.

271
00:16:59,890 --> 00:17:02,600
For the first time in my life...

272
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:05,230
...after my dad left me...

273
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:10,570
...and then getting arrested for stealing those birds...

274
00:17:10,940 --> 00:17:14,530
...and then the whole punctured-lung thing.

275
00:17:15,860 --> 00:17:19,320
It's still really hard to take deep breaths in cold weather...

276
00:17:19,530 --> 00:17:23,450
...but with Alice, all that stuff kind of went away.

277
00:17:24,750 --> 00:17:29,130
And now it's gone, and I don't know why.

278
00:17:30,540 --> 00:17:35,090
Ugh. Well, I can tell you why. It's because of me.

279
00:17:35,970 --> 00:17:39,470
But you know what? I only did it because I love you, okay?

280
00:17:41,760 --> 00:17:46,350
- What?     - Um, I kind of had a little chat with Alice...

281
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:49,730
...and I sort of made her see why you two shouldn't be together.

282
00:17:49,900 --> 00:17:53,230
And you'll see it too, one day. You really, really will.

283
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:55,940
Wait a minute. This is because of you?

284
00:17:56,110 --> 00:17:57,150
Okay...

285
00:17:57,320 --> 00:18:00,490
Wait, no. My mother didn't want us to be together...

286
00:18:00,660 --> 00:18:03,580
...but the worst thing she did was tie me to the porch.

287
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:05,790
Okay, but...

288
00:18:05,950 --> 00:18:09,540
I came to you because I thought you'd understand.

289
00:18:09,710 --> 00:18:12,000
Oh, no!

290
00:18:14,630 --> 00:18:16,800
I would storm out of here...

291
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:20,800
...if I had some money or a place to go.

292
00:18:26,810 --> 00:18:29,020
Oh, my God! The millionaire's here!

293
00:18:29,190 --> 00:18:31,230
Oh, my God!

294
00:18:36,030 --> 00:18:38,530
Guys, please. I'm just gonna have dinner with him.

295
00:18:38,700 --> 00:18:43,490
Okay, just because he buys you dinner does not mean you owe him anything.

296
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:46,120
I know.

297
00:18:47,370 --> 00:18:49,960
Okay, then get the lobster.

298
00:18:53,750 --> 00:18:54,840
- Hey.     - Hi.

299
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,210
- Hi.     - Hey.

300
00:18:56,380 --> 00:18:57,590
Hello.

301
00:18:58,420 --> 00:19:01,010
Hey, how much cash you got in your pocket right now?

302
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:07,600
And that's why I'm not inviting you in for a drink. Bye.

303
00:19:07,770 --> 00:19:09,810
Why not? Hey, come in for drink.

304
00:19:11,350 --> 00:19:13,400
- Where do you wanna go?     - You like pizza?

305
00:19:13,560 --> 00:19:17,020
- Oh, that sounds great.     - I know a great little place.

306
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:23,070

307
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:25,240
You're not paying for the pizza.

308
00:19:25,410 --> 00:19:28,950
Come on, it's only fair. You paid for the flight.

309
00:19:29,580 --> 00:19:30,710
Is that enough lira?

310
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:33,210
Uh, I'd throw another 1000 on that.

311
00:19:33,830 --> 00:19:36,290
- How much is that?     - That's about 60 cents.

312
00:19:47,810 --> 00:19:49,930
Every night!

313
00:19:51,730 --> 00:19:54,020
You don't need to smoke.

314
00:19:54,190 --> 00:19:56,690
Cigarettes don't control you.

315
00:19:56,860 --> 00:20:00,530
You are a strong, confident woman...

316
00:20:00,690 --> 00:20:03,490
...who does not need to smoke.

317
00:20:03,660 --> 00:20:06,950
A strong, confident woman...

318
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:10,330
...who does not need to smoke.

319
00:20:11,290 --> 00:20:13,120
So can I.

320
00:20:19,130 --> 00:20:20,760
Hey, Frank.

321
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:25,800
Look, I know that you think I did this totally evil thing.

322
00:20:25,970 --> 00:20:27,430
But I so didn't.

323
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:31,640
Someone's here who can explain this better than I can.

324
00:20:33,100 --> 00:20:34,690
We can go look.

325
00:20:37,150 --> 00:20:38,310
Hi, Frank.

326
00:20:42,030 --> 00:20:45,280
Hi, Mrs. Knight.

327
00:20:47,740 --> 00:20:49,780
Phoebe's right, Frank.

328
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:54,330
It's hard to hear, but it would've been wrong to go through with it.

329
00:20:54,580 --> 00:20:56,250
I was being selfish.

330
00:20:56,420 --> 00:21:00,290
Even though we want the same things right now...

331
00:21:00,460 --> 00:21:03,340
...in the future, we may not.

332
00:21:04,470 --> 00:21:07,010
- Is that what it is?     - Yes, but not just that.

333
00:21:07,180 --> 00:21:09,300
Right, not just that.

334
00:21:12,180 --> 00:21:17,520
Even though we love each other as much as we do...

335
00:21:18,190 --> 00:21:19,650
...nonetheless...

336
00:21:22,070 --> 00:21:23,860
- Nonetheless.     - Nonetheless.

337
00:21:28,950 --> 00:21:31,200
You're too young...

338
00:21:31,700 --> 00:21:35,040
...to really know what you want.

339
00:21:35,210 --> 00:21:37,210
That's right, exactly.

340
00:21:39,580 --> 00:21:41,670
That's a goodbye kiss. That's good.

341
00:21:44,010 --> 00:21:45,380
Bye-bye.

342
00:21:46,510 --> 00:21:50,850
The important thing is, is that you see what I'm saying.

343
00:21:51,510 --> 00:21:53,720
This is clearly wrong.

344
00:21:55,310 --> 00:21:57,770
I've decided I'm gonna let this happen.

345
00:21:58,560 --> 00:22:00,860
Okay, can I just get my purse?

346
00:22:01,020 --> 00:22:03,650
Okay, all right, good.

347
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:11,120
Cigarettes don't control you.

348
00:22:11,280 --> 00:22:14,370
You are a strong, confident woman...

349
00:22:14,540 --> 00:22:17,410
...who does not need to smoke.

350
00:22:19,420 --> 00:22:22,840
Joey's your best friend.

351
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:27,550
You wanna make him a cheese sandwich every day.

352
00:22:29,590 --> 00:22:35,060
And you also wanna buy him hundreds of dollars worth of pants.

